Usage of edicta-live:
  -agent-id string
    	agent id on edictad's allowlist
  -agent-key-file string
    	agent Ed25519 key: file of exactly 32 raw seed bytes, mode 0600
  -api-token-file string
    	file with edictad's bearer token (authorize; also record unless --record-token-file)
  -api-url string
    	edictad base URL, for example http://127.0.0.1:8080
  -archive-url string
    	fast mode: base URL of the archive edictad writes, read for the anchor intent
  -asset string
    	asset id (coingecko id; label for kraken) (default "celestia")
  -bridge-addr string
    	bridge node JSON-RPC address (reads, proofs)
  -bridge-tls
    	use TLS to the bridge node
  -bridge-token-file string
    	file with the bridge node auth token
  -chain-id string
    	optional: refuse a node on another chain id
  -confirm-delay duration
    	wait before the second status query of that final check; at most --rebroadcast-every (0 = default 2s)
  -crosscheck-bridge value
    	crosscheck: an independent bridge node address (at least two; repeatable)
  -crosscheck-tls
    	crosscheck: TLS to the --crosscheck-bridge nodes
  -crosscheck-token-file string
    	crosscheck: auth token file shared by the --crosscheck-bridge nodes
  -da string
    	data availability mode edictad runs: blob or fibre (default "blob")
  -down-addr string
    	destination when the price moves down
  -down-amount uint
    	amount in base units (utia) when down
  -dry-run
    	do everything except broadcast the transfer and record it
  -evidence-file string
    	also write the evidence JSON to this file
  -executor-ed25519-file string
    	executor Ed25519 key for record requests: 32 raw seed bytes, mode 0600; its public key must be in edictad's executor_keys
  -executor-key string
    	executor key name in that keyring
  -executor-keyring-dir string
    	executor keyring directory (file backend; not the Recorder's)
  -executor-passphrase-file string
    	file with the keyring passphrase
  -executor-passphrase-prompt
    	ask for the keyring passphrase on the terminal, no echo
  -fast
    	sign a pending reference edictad's Recorder returns, after checking its anchor intent through --grpc-addr (and --bridge-addr for da=blob); needs --archive-url
  -fee uint
    	fee in base units (utia); 0 derives it from the node's minimum gas price
  -fee-margin string
    	decimal factor on the node's minimum gas price when --fee is 0 (default 1.2)
  -gas-limit uint
    	gas limit of the transfer (default 150000)
  -gate-id string
    	pin the gate id (default: learned from edictad)
  -gate-pubkey string
    	pin the gate Ed25519 public key, 64 hex (default: learned from edictad; pinning is strongly advised)
  -gen-recipient-key string
    	create a new recipient key file at this path (mode 0600, must not exist) and add it
  -grpc-addr string
    	consensus node gRPC address (account, broadcast, tx lookup)
  -grpc-tls
    	use TLS to the consensus gRPC endpoint
  -grpc-token-file string
    	file with the consensus gRPC token
  -inclusion string
    	inclusion check: self (same operator), light (validator signatures) or crosscheck (default "self")
  -indexer-lag-blocks int
    	blocks past the timeout height the status node may lag before a missing tx counts as lost (0 = default 3)
  -json
    	print the evidence as JSON instead of text
  -kraken-pair string
    	kraken: ticker pair (default "TIAUSD")
  -mandate-hash string
    	hash of the gate's mandate, 64 hex, carried as the commitment's mandate_ref; required with --fast
  -max-app-version uint
    	compatibility check upper bound (0 = default)
  -max-decisions int
    	stop after this many decisions (default 1)
  -max-fee uint
    	the executor refuses to sign a fee above this (default 1000)
  -min-app-version uint
    	compatibility check lower bound (0 = default)
  -namespace string
    	pin the blob namespace, 58 hex (default: learned from edictad)
  -poll-interval duration
    	price poll interval (default 30s)
  -price-base-url string
    	override the price source base URL
  -price-source string
    	price source: coingecko or kraken (default "coingecko")
  -publish-wait duration
    	bound of one publication attempt (0 = SDK default)
  -quote string
    	quote currency, upper case (default "USD")
  -reason string
    	optional free-text reason carried in the context
  -rebroadcast-every duration
    	resend interval of the same signed bytes (default 10s)
  -recipient value
